 "note": "Trimmed gate (three tiers) + C7 SNR. C7.injected (fail, sim only) = pre-integration noise the vibration pass ADDED, bounded by the loudest real flight total; C7.noise_eff (warn) = total; C7.snr report. Raw fleet1 flights already carry 0.17-0.34 m/s^2 of surviving noise from the simulated controller, the pass adds ~0.08. Rule: every real bag passes the FAIL tier with zero warns. FAIL = C5.finite/magnitude/level/lowband + SEG; WARN = C3.exist/width/responsive, C2.gaussian/breathe, C4.contrast; the rest report-only. The earlier C0.shaft_steady check and its downstream-annotation logic were removed: it compared the sim's rotor sidecar against a real-aircraft spread that cannot be measured without motor telemetry (the '7-70x' figure compared a whole-mission p5-p95 against a 60 s line width; like for like the real shaft moves ~4% over a mission vs the sim's 16% instantaneous / ~6% at 1 s smoothing), and add_vibration.py now phase-integrates the 1 s-smoothed shaft. Known cosmetic: on PAS bags the census can lock onto the simulator's own narrow 23-27 Hz line (present in the RAW bag at ~7 dB, a tenth of a tone's energy), so C3.exist/width/contrast on fleet bags may describe that line rather than the 1x tone at ~43 Hz; they are warn/report tier for that reason. Line width on fleet bags (~10-13 Hz after smoothing) is slow tens-of-seconds throttle motion of the simulated aircraft, not chatter; accepted as a warn.",
